  data: {
    LLM: "Memory is everything. Pay close attention to what other players are asking for, even when it isn't your turn. If Player A asks Player B for 7s, you now know both players likely have 7s.\n\nThe 'Re-Fishing' Tactic: If you know someone just fished a card you originally held, wait until they've collected a few more of that rank before asking them. Let them do the work for you.\n\nQuantity Bluffing: Ask for a rank you only have one of, but do it confidently as if you are completing a Book. This clears the 'Ocean' of that rank as others stop fishing for it, thinking you've already cornered the market.",
    Player: "Memory is everything. Pay close attention to what other players are asking for, even when it isn't your turn. If Player A asks Player B for 7s, you now know both players likely have 7s.\n\nThe 'Re-Fishing' Tactic: If you know someone just fished a card you originally held, wait until they've collected a few more of that rank before asking them. Let them do the work for you.\n\nQuantity Bluffing: Ask for a rank you only have one of, but do it confidently as if you are completing a Book. This clears the 'Ocean' of that rank as others stop fishing for it, thinking you've already cornered the market.",
